; v4 wire family. Quote remains independently versioned; pool/content/arbitration
; messages carry their own strict major and are not decoded as older payloads.
; This v4 was hard-switched six times before launch: first RefundTemplateTxID became
; the unified pool correlation ID, then 003/004 were switched to one payment
; sequence authorizing an ordered content-hash batch and one delivery package
; atomically carrying the same batch (see content.cddl), then 005 was
; switched to the minimal payment credential — authorization hash plus Buyer
; transaction signature — with both sides deterministically rebuilding the state
; transaction locally (see payment.cddl), then 007 switched to the
; five-element Claim/payload custody request and five-element Result response
; with independent candidate reconstruction, then 007 was hard-switched
; again to paid arbitration: a four-element Kind 9 receipt response carrying a
; three-element Receipt (Claim ID, positive arbiter amount, arbitration
; transaction signature) signed over [4, 9, exact_receipt_cbor] (see
; arbitration.cddl), and finally 008 added Buyer custody retrieval: a
; five-element Kind 10 Buyer-signed request routed by ArbitrationClaimID plus
; a four-element Kind 11 response embedding the exact persisted Kind 8/9
; bytes (see arbitration.cddl). Only post-switch structures are accepted;
; pre-switch v4 bytes, legacy aliases, and any dual-shape decoding do not
; exist in this protocol version.
wire-family = "bitfs.protocol.v4"
